{"content":[{"c":["FOWLER*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["One who traps or shoots wild birds. The catching of birds for pets, food, and sacrifices was the business of the fowler. This was done by the use of a bow and arrow, a sling, or a net (",{"href":"?bref=Pr.1.17","r":"Pr.1.17","rawR":"Pr.1.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.1.17","value":"Pr.1.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prv 1:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.12.13","r":"Ezek.12.13","rawR":"Ezek.12.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.12.13","value":"Ezek.12.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 12:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.17.20","r":"Ezek.17.20","rawR":"Ezek.17.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.17.20","value":"Ezek.17.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"17:20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Hos.7.12","r":"Hos.7.12","rawR":"Hos.7.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hos.7.12","value":"Hos.7.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Hos 7:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Hos.9.8","r":"Hos.9.8","rawR":"Hos.9.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hos.9.8","value":"Hos.9.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:8"},"). Other methods included the use of bird lime, a sticky substance to which birds adhere, and a throw stick that broke the birds’ legs. Fowlers lay in wait near their trap, placing the captured birds in a basket (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.5.26-27","r":"Jer.5.26-27","rawR":"Jer.5.26-27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.5.26-27","value":"Jer.5.26-27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 5:26-27"},"). The term “fowler” appears also as a metaphor for wicked men who trap other men (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.91.3","r":"Ps.91.3","rawR":"Ps.91.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.91.3","value":"Ps.91.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 91:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.124.7","r":"Ps.124.7","rawR":"Ps.124.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.124.7","value":"Ps.124.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"124:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.5.26","r":"Jer.5.26","rawR":"Jer.5.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.5.26","value":"Jer.5.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 5:26"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Hos.9.8","r":"Hos.9.8","rawR":"Hos.9.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hos.9.8","value":"Hos.9.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Hos 9:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Hunting_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Hunting_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Hunting_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Hunting"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Fowler","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Prv 1:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Pr.1.17","rawQueryValue":"Pr.1.17","sourceRefExact":"Pr.1.17"},{"anchorText":"Ez 12:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.12.13","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.12.13","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.12.13"},{"anchorText":"17:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.17.20","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.17.20","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.17.20"},{"anchorText":"Hos 7:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Hos.7.12","rawQueryValue":"Hos.7.12","sourceRefExact":"Hos.7.12"},{"anchorText":"9:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Hos.9.8","rawQueryValue":"Hos.9.8","sourceRefExact":"Hos.9.8"},{"anchorText":"Jer 5:26-27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.5.26-27","rawQueryValue":"Jer.5.26-27","sourceRefExact":"Jer.5.26-27"},{"anchorText":"Pss 91:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.91.3","rawQueryValue":"Ps.91.3","sourceRefExact":"Ps.91.3"},{"anchorText":"124:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.124.7","rawQueryValue":"Ps.124.7","sourceRefExact":"Ps.124.7"},{"anchorText":"Jer 5:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.5.26","rawQueryValue":"Jer.5.26"